#
# litellm-oss — the DIRECT dependencies of our LiteLLM gateway image (the input of requirements.lock).
#
# WHY NOT `litellm[proxy]`. litellm 1.109.1's `proxy` extra declares
#   Requires-Dist: litellm-enterprise==0.1.82 ; extra == 'proxy'
# and litellm-enterprise is `LicenseRef-Proprietary`. So the extra is spelled out here instead,
# copied from litellm-1.109.1.dist-info/METADATA (python 3.13 markers), with these left out:
#   litellm-enterprise   proprietary: the reason this image exists
#   restrictedpython     ZPL-2.1, used only by the custom-code guardrail sandbox, which the OS never configures
#   soundfile            a binding to the native libsndfile (LGPL-2.1), which the image does not ship;
#                        only AWS Transcribe pass-through cost tracking uses it (patches/0001)
#   psycopg-binary       LGPL-3.0, and bundles its own libpq/OpenSSL/Kerberos build; kept out with
#                        --no-emit-package (lock.sh). The pure-Python `psycopg` stays (below), on the
#                        system libpq5 (PostgreSQL licence) the Dockerfile installs.
#   hf-xet               a dependency of huggingface-hub that embeds MPL-2.0 Rust crates; optional there
#                        (Xet storage downloads only), kept out with --no-emit-package
# Versions: lock.sh resolves against the exact versions the upstream image
# ghcr.io/berriai/litellm-database:1.109.1@sha256:932c5444… ships (upstream-constraints.txt), so the
# gateway runs the library versions production ran, minus the packages left out.
#
# Named .in, not requirements*.txt, on purpose: the repo-wide licence gate resolves every
# requirements*.txt with plain pip, which would re-add psycopg through litellm-proxy-extras. This
# image is gated on what is ACTUALLY INSTALLED instead: scripts/license-gate-image.mjs.
#
# Regenerate the lock: images/extensions/litellm-oss/lock.sh   (never hand-edit requirements.lock)
litellm==1.109.1

